From 13bff3ad95526f46a39b1fdbd2eaf3be28e9af72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TomBolger <49487944+TomBolger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:00:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] comm/ble/ancs: drop notifications removed from iOS while
 disconnected

A notification removed from the iOS notification center while the watch
was away stayed in its history: removals only arrive while connected.

When the notification center is mirrored, collect the UIDs iOS tells of for
10 s after subscribing to the Notification Source, which is when iOS
re-sends its whole notification center, and then have the stored iOS
notifications it no longer has dropped. Pre-existing notifications are also
fetched on the first connection after boot, so that the history starts
with what is on the phone.

The snapshot is given up, keeping every stored notification, if more UIDs
come than it holds, if a notification event was dropped on the way to
KernelMain, or if the session ends first.

Assisted-by: LLM
